From 26f7f1d353efbd110dcbb41bf79431f58f7aba9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel <kernel@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:12:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] ik2: decode loop host waits behind IK2_K_S* (default off)

- IK2_K_SOVL: drafter context rows queued behind the step's launches before the host waits (event wait on the
  step's results); a window's rows for all positions where write_ahead_ok; timing-only syncs dropped
- IK2_K_SWIN: window queued straight behind the drafter, embedding rows decoded on the device (embd_rows) from
  the drafter's device tokens and a pinned mapped table: one host wait per round
- IK2_K_SSAMP: nth_element+sort (partial_sort's order) and a bounded Gumbel pick: same tokens, ~2x faster host sampling
---
 docs/INKLING2.md        |  13 +++
 src/ik2/ik2_draft.cu    |  17 ++-
 src/ik2/ik2_draft.hpp   |  13 +++
 src/ik2/ik2_kernels.cu  |  23 ++++
 src/ik2/ik2_kernels.cuh |   6 +
 src/ik2/ik2_main.cu     | 253 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 6 files changed, 272 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/INKLING2.md b/docs/INKLING2.md
index b003bde0..3cf53ac2 100644
--- a/docs/INKLING2.md
+++ b/docs/INKLING2.md
@@ -413,6 +413,19 @@ same tokens: new code 201 / 124, a tool call 201 / 124, an edit 210 / 124, a 900
 there 114 -> 154 tok/s (plain 102) with the tokens' queries on a key's rows read once and the drafter's attention on
 the tensor cores (a draft there 6.1 -> 2.0 ms, a window of 5 23.2 -> 17.4 ms).
 
+**The host's waits** (`IK2_K_S*`, off by default: every step as before). A drafted round waited three times - for the
+drafts, for the window, and after the drafter's context rows (timing only) - and a plain token twice, the GPU idle
+each time while the host woke up, sampled and queued the next launches. `IK2_K_SOVL=1` queues the drafter's context
+rows behind the step's launches before the host waits (a window's for all its positions where the kept rows come out
+the same: a Q8_0 drafter with the whole context; the others are written again when kept) and waits on an event after
+the step's own results, so the GPU writes them while the host samples; the timing waits go (a step is timed until its
+tokens are the host's). `IK2_K_SWIN=1` queues the window straight behind the drafter, its embedding rows decoded on
+the device from the drafts the drafter left there (a pinned, mapped copy of the table, ~0.5 GiB of RAM; Q8_0 / Q6_K
+/ Q5_0 / NVFP4 / IQ3_XXS / IQ4_XS tables, not with `IK2_ABLATE`): one wait a round. `IK2_K_SSAMP=1` samples sooner
+on the host (the candidates ordered with nth_element and sort - partial_sort's order - and the Gumbel pick stopped
+where no lower token's noise reaches the best). The tokens are the same with or without them. HIP has no
+conditional graph nodes (ROCm 7.1's `hipGraphNodeType` list), so the width stays the host's choice.
+
 To run it (one GPU):
 
     python tools/strata_tokenizer.py --gguf Inkling-2-Mini-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf --out ik2 \
