+// IK2_K_SOVL: may a window's context rows be written for every one of its positions before the drafts kept are known?
+// Yes where a row's values do not depend on the rows written with it (Q8_0 matrices: q8_tile's columns apart) and
+// no position a later step reads is overwritten (the layer without a window holds the whole context; the windowed
+// layers' rings of 2048 hold their 1023 and a window more) - the rows past the kept ones are written again when
+// their positions are kept, and no step reads a position at or past its anchor's.
+bool write_ahead_ok(const Drafter* d);
